		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5183&amp;p=37500#p37500"><![CDATA[
Hello everyone, and thank you very much for joining the forum.<br><br>I'm sharing my problem to see if anyone else has had a similar experience.<br><br>I have a hotspot that I can access from any of my digital devices (TYT9600 and 878 UV2+) without any problems.<br><br>I just purchased a Retevis RT3s and installed opengd77, but I can't seem to "open" the hotspot when I press the PTT button on my new walkie-talkie. I've tried everything, including inserting the TYT9600's cocodeplug, since it works on this device, but I can't open the HS. I've also tried correcting the hotspot frequency, but to no avail. It doesn't receive anything, and as soon as I move it from its current location, the "Time Out" message starts appearing on the Retevis screen, so I assume there's no need to move it. I'm starting to think the modem is broken, but... Has anyone else had something similar happen to them...?<br><br>Thank you all so much!!<br><br>73s.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8783">ea2faw</a> — Mon Jun 16, 2025 10:54 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
